  "strings": {
    "getting-started.campaign.title": "Getting Started",
    "getting-started.campaign.description": "An interactive orientation. It explains Adventures by making you use Adventures. Skipping is a valid choice. So is not skipping.",
    "getting-started.var_first_take.label": "First take",
    "getting-started.start.text": "Welcome to SubZeroDev.Adventures.\n\nThis probably requires an explanation.",
    "getting-started.start.choice_explain": "What the fuck is this?",
    "getting-started.start.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.explain_engine.text": "Adventures is a small platform for playing — and building — interactive stories called campaigns.\n\nA campaign is a graph: nodes with text, choices that branch, state that persists across choices, and achievements that fire when you do something notable. No account required to read it.\n\nThis conversation? Also a campaign. We are using the platform to explain the platform.",
    "getting-started.explain_engine.choice_continue": "Keep going.",
    "getting-started.explain_engine.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.branching_demo.text": "The engine lets a story branch based on what you pick. Here's a branch. It doesn't matter which way you go.",
    "getting-started.branching_demo.choice_powerful": "This sounds incredibly powerful.",
    "getting-started.branching_demo.choice_complicated": "This sounds unnecessarily complicated.",
    "getting-started.branching_demo.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.branch_converge.text": "Both lead here.\n\nSee? Choices.\n\n(You said this sounds {first_take}. We'll remember that — state persists across the whole run, not just the one choice you made it in.)",
    "getting-started.branch_converge.choice_continue": "Continue.",
    "getting-started.branch_converge.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.node_kinds.text": "(unshown — a bare `auto` pass-through node; see achievements_intro's opening line)",
    "getting-started.achievements_intro.text": "Getting to this line took one extra step you didn't click anything for — a node with no choices, that just forwards you to the next one. If you didn't notice, that's correct. That's what those are for.\n\nSpeaking of things that happen without a form to fill out: the engine also tracks achievements — unlocked mid-story, the moment some condition becomes true, whether or not anyone announces it.\n\nFor example. You're satisfying one right now.",
    "getting-started.achievements_intro.choice_what": "Wait, what did I just unlock?",
    "getting-started.achievements_intro.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.achievements_explained.text": "Achievement Unlocked: Achievement Unlocked.\n\nYou learned that achievements exist by receiving an achievement for learning that achievements exist.",
    "getting-started.achievements_explained.choice_continue": "Neat.",
    "getting-started.achievements_explained.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.content_composition_intro.text": "Not every campaign is a sealed island, either. Content can be composed — extra nodes and choices, injected onto an existing graph from a separate file, without anyone touching the original.\n\nCampaigns aren't necessarily isolated. Other content can—",
    "getting-started.content_composition_intro.choice_shrug": "—sure. Moving on.",
    "getting-started.content_composition_intro.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.campaign_shapes.text": "Here's the part people miss: a campaign isn't just \"choose your own adventure.\" It's a decision graph with content, state, branching, persistence, and achievements. That shape can hold a comedy. It can also hold a game, a how-to guide, a troubleshooting flow, an internal runbook, onboarding for literally anything, or family tech support.",
    "getting-started.campaign_shapes.choice_example": "Show me the family tech support one.",
    "getting-started.campaign_shapes.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.tv_support_2.text": "Case file: \"My television doesn't work.\"\n\nIs it turned on?",
    "getting-started.tv_support_2.choice_yes": "Yes.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_2.choice_no": "No.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_3.text": "Does it say NO SIGNAL?",
    "getting-started.tv_support_3.choice_yes": "Yes.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_3.choice_no": "No.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_4.text": "Turn it on.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_4.choice_continue": "...Oh.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_5.text": "Check the input source. It's HDMI 2. It's always HDMI 2.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_5.choice_continue": "Continue.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_6.text": "Unplug it, count to ten, plug it back in. This resolves sixty percent of problems, one hundred percent of the time.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_6.choice_continue": "Continue.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_end_ok.text": "That's the whole runbook. It's not funnier than your actual runbooks. That's kind of the point.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_end_ok.choice_continue": "Good. Continue.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_end_ok.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.tv_support_end_maybe.text": "Nothing worked.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_end_maybe.choice_call": "Call Ben.",
    "getting-started.tv_support_end_maybe.choice_continue": "Give up gracefully and continue.",
    "getting-started.escalation_ending.text": "Ben does not pick up.\n\nThe graph has exhausted its usefulness. So has Ben.",
    "getting-started.self_hosting_intro.text": "Longer term, campaigns won't only be ours. The plan is for you to author your own graphs and decide how they're exposed — public, private, shared by a link, or fully self-hosted. Some of that exists today. Some of it doesn't yet. We're telling you which is which instead of pretending otherwise.",
    "getting-started.self_hosting_intro.choice_continue": "Noted.",
    "getting-started.self_hosting_intro.choice_skip": "Skip Intro...",
    "getting-started.closing.text": "That's Adventures: a graph engine wearing a trenchcoat.\n\nIn the last few minutes you've used branching, persistent state, an achievement, a node kind nobody named out loud, and — if you went looking — a small unauthorized side quest. There's nothing left to explain. Only things left to play.",
    "getting-started.closing.choice_finish": "See the shelf.",
    "getting-started.complete_ending.text": "Tutorial complete.\n\nAchievement unlocked: Actually Reads the Manual. We genuinely did not expect anyone to get this far.\n\nGo pick a real one.",
    "getting-started.skip_ending.text": "Skipped.\n\nNo judgment. Well — a little.",
    "getting-started.achievement_never.name": "Never Reads the Manual",
    "getting-started.achievement_never.description": "Skipped the tutorial. You'll figure it out. Probably.",
    "getting-started.achievement_tried.name": "Tried Reading the Manual",
    "getting-started.achievement_tried.description": "You made an effort. That's more concerning, actually.",
    "getting-started.achievement_actually.name": "Actually Reads the Manual",
    "getting-started.achievement_actually.description": "We genuinely did not expect anyone to get this far.",
    "getting-started.achievement_meta.name": "Achievement Unlocked: Achievement Unlocked",
    "getting-started.achievement_meta.description": "You learned that achievements exist by receiving an achievement for learning that achievements exist.",
    "getting-started.achievement_escalation.name": "The Escalation Path",
    "getting-started.achievement_escalation.description": "The graph has exhausted its usefulness. So has Ben."
  }
}
